WEBVTT

00:02:01.980 --> 00:02:03.370
Now, it's the Bats!

00:02:03.370 --> 00:02:05.060
It's the top of the ninth inning and the Bats have two outs with the bases loaded.

00:02:05.060 --> 00:02:08.350
Their closer, Shigeno, takes the mound.

00:02:08.780 --> 00:02:11.270
However, Shigeno hasn't been at his best lately.

00:02:11.560 --> 00:02:14.760
Can he defend their one run lead?

00:02:19.250 --> 00:02:19.950
Ball!

00:02:19.950 --> 00:02:20.660
Ball four!

00:02:25.330 --> 00:02:26.330
<i>Dammit!</i>

00:02:27.980 --> 00:02:30.750
<i>I tried to hit the corner, but...</i>

00:02:35.440 --> 00:02:37.740
It's gone!

00:02:37.740 --> 00:02:40.440
Shigeno fails to get the save again!

00:02:40.440 --> 00:02:45.100
The pennant is just in front of their eyes and the Bats have made no progress today either!

00:02:45.100 --> 00:02:46.220
<i>Dammit!</i>

00:02:46.610 --> 00:02:50.220
<i>I've been so caught up in perfecting my control...</i>

00:02:50.220 --> 00:02:54.060
<i>that my pitches end up being easy to read instead of being subtle.</i>

00:02:54.710 --> 00:02:56.230
<i>Just a little more.</i>

00:02:56.850 --> 00:03:00.000
<i>I'm just a step away from perfecting it.</i>

00:03:15.760 --> 00:03:17.130
Yo, Shigeno.

00:03:17.130 --> 00:03:19.430
You're still training at this hour?

00:03:20.490 --> 00:03:21.420
Yeah.

00:03:21.420 --> 00:03:24.310
Are you still hung up on today's loss?

00:03:24.310 --> 00:03:27.200
You're really wearing a glum face. There!

00:03:27.200 --> 00:03:28.140
Shut up!

00:03:28.140 --> 00:03:29.760
You seem really frustrated.

00:03:29.760 --> 00:03:32.320
You should take a break.

00:03:32.320 --> 00:03:34.250
Hey, how about we go for a cruise?

00:03:34.250 --> 00:03:37.150
Let's have some fun on our day off tomorrow!

00:03:37.150 --> 00:03:39.130
With just three guys?

00:03:39.130 --> 00:03:41.300
That's a lame cruise.

00:03:41.300 --> 00:03:43.570
Of course not.

00:03:43.880 --> 00:03:47.120
We'll try and invite some hot girls too.

00:03:49.600 --> 00:03:50.870
All right.

00:03:50.870 --> 00:03:52.790
I'll join you guys for a bit.

00:03:53.870 --> 00:03:55.010
Nice!

00:03:55.010 --> 00:03:56.060
All right!

00:03:56.060 --> 00:03:57.000
Hey, Maki.

00:03:57.000 --> 00:03:58.880
Do you have any plans later?

00:03:58.880 --> 00:03:59.760
Not really.

00:03:59.760 --> 00:04:03.180
Then, do you want to stop by the batting cages?

00:04:03.180 --> 00:04:04.630
I have a free ticket.

00:04:04.630 --> 00:04:06.440
No way! I'll pass!

00:04:06.440 --> 00:04:07.740
Why?

00:04:07.740 --> 00:04:08.970
It's free! Free!

00:04:09.260 --> 00:04:11.750
Because you get serious too easily.

00:04:11.750 --> 00:04:16.440
You'll probably start saying things like, "I won't leave until I can hit all the balls," or start whining.

00:04:18.470 --> 00:04:21.350
Just go have fun by yourself.

00:04:21.350 --> 00:04:26.180
I'm not like you. I can't dedicate my whole body and soul to softball.

00:04:26.180 --> 00:04:27.780
What does that mean!?

00:04:28.000 --> 00:04:30.630
You make it sound like I'm addicted to softball!

00:04:30.630 --> 00:04:33.790
Not "sound like." You are.

00:04:34.040 --> 00:04:35.620
Yeah. Yeah.

00:04:44.100 --> 00:04:47.960
That Maki... Saying whatever she likes...

00:04:49.060 --> 00:04:50.590
<i>Damn!</i>

00:04:51.460 --> 00:04:54.980
It looks like softball is Shimi-chan's boyfriend.

00:04:55.270 --> 00:04:58.560
But does she really have no interest in men?

00:04:58.560 --> 00:05:00.820
It really seems like it.

00:05:00.820 --> 00:05:07.530
Well, it's really complicated, but there is a guy that's kind of like a boyfriend.

00:05:07.530 --> 00:05:09.260
Huh!? No way!

00:05:09.260 --> 00:05:11.530
Hey, what's he like!? What's he like!?

00:05:11.530 --> 00:05:13.990
Simply putting it, he's addicted to baseball too.

00:05:13.990 --> 00:05:15.780
He's in America at the moment.

00:05:15.780 --> 00:05:17.960
That means they're in a very long distance relationship.

00:05:17.960 --> 00:05:18.940
Yeah...

00:05:18.940 --> 00:05:23.500
But she let him go without making any sort of arrangement.

00:05:23.500 --> 00:05:26.050
It doesn't seem like she's confessed to him either.

00:05:26.050 --> 00:05:28.170
Wow. That's complicated.

00:05:28.170 --> 00:05:29.630
I know.

00:05:29.630 --> 00:05:32.780
And he's also aiming for the Majors on top of that.

00:05:32.780 --> 00:05:34.730
Who knows when he's going to come back.

00:05:34.730 --> 00:05:40.170
But, that sounds more like they're baseball buddies than a couple.

00:05:40.170 --> 00:05:41.190
That's true.

00:05:41.910 --> 00:05:43.450
Yeah.

00:05:51.490 --> 00:05:54.950
<i>I wonder if Honda's doing well over there.</i>

00:05:58.380 --> 00:06:00.090
Oh, it's from Maki.

00:06:00.090 --> 00:06:01.090
Hello?

00:06:01.320 --> 00:06:02.800
Hey, Kaoru?

00:06:02.800 --> 00:06:04.580
It's about tomorrow.

00:06:04.580 --> 00:06:10.010
We've decided to have a joint training practice game with another university.

00:06:10.700 --> 00:06:11.430
Really?

00:06:12.230 --> 00:06:13.460
Okay. Okay.

00:06:13.460 --> 00:06:14.450
Okay. Okay.

00:06:14.450 --> 00:06:17.220
I see! Then I'll see you tomorrow!

00:06:18.300 --> 00:06:19.260
All right!

00:06:19.260 --> 00:06:20.600
It's a game! A game!

00:06:20.600 --> 00:06:21.730
All right!

00:06:21.730 --> 00:06:23.650
I'm going to do my best!

00:06:27.600 --> 00:06:29.780
Good morning!

00:06:30.460 --> 00:06:31.450
Huh?

00:06:31.900 --> 00:06:34.390
W-What's with those outfits?

00:06:35.120 --> 00:06:37.040
Morning, Kaoru.

00:06:38.000 --> 00:06:39.770
W-Wait! What are you doing!?

00:06:39.770 --> 00:06:42.110
Misaki! Asami! Let go!

00:06:43.700 --> 00:06:46.400
Makiko! Don't we have a joint training session today!?

00:06:46.400 --> 00:06:47.440
We do.

00:06:47.440 --> 00:06:51.240
We're going to have a joint training session about love for your sake.

00:06:51.240 --> 00:06:52.010
Huh?

00:06:52.420 --> 00:06:57.680
We can't sit still, because we're really worried about your future.

00:06:57.680 --> 00:07:02.400
So we decided to give you a helping hand in getting you a guy.

00:07:02.400 --> 00:07:06.820
We've gathered some good-looking guys from a famous university, so do your best!

00:07:07.070 --> 00:07:08.880
Y-You tricked me!

00:07:08.880 --> 00:07:10.490
Stop squirming.

00:07:11.040 --> 00:07:15.330
Shigeno-kun probably has a girlfriend with a nice body in America too.

00:07:17.090 --> 00:07:19.390
That's not possible!

00:07:23.930 --> 00:07:25.850
So you're 18?

00:07:25.850 --> 00:07:27.270
You're hot!

00:07:27.270 --> 00:07:29.340
I-It's a bit hard to breathe.

00:07:29.340 --> 00:07:31.510
Why do they like him so much?

00:07:31.510 --> 00:07:32.760
Like I'd know.

00:07:35.550 --> 00:07:37.420
Hey, we're almost there.

00:07:38.060 --> 00:07:39.000
Thank you!

00:07:39.000 --> 00:07:41.710
You saved me by giving me a lift.

00:07:41.710 --> 00:07:43.140
You're getting off already?

00:07:43.140 --> 00:07:46.020
That's boring.

00:07:48.190 --> 00:07:49.790
Now, get out. Get out.

00:07:49.790 --> 00:07:51.490
It's a short walk from here.

00:07:51.490 --> 00:07:54.360
I hope it's a good game.

00:07:54.360 --> 00:07:55.930
See you, Shigeno.

00:07:58.310 --> 00:07:59.410
Shigeno!

00:08:04.920 --> 00:08:05.950
All right.

00:08:05.950 --> 00:08:07.880
We got rid of that nuisance.

00:08:08.270 --> 00:08:09.730
Hey, where do you want to go?

00:08:09.730 --> 00:08:11.380
Requests, please!

00:08:11.380 --> 00:08:12.630
We want to go home.

00:08:23.910 --> 00:08:25.920
Oh, here it is.

00:08:32.450 --> 00:08:37.410
<i>Come to think of it, the last time I saw a Major League game was when I was a kid.</i>

00:08:55.300 --> 00:08:58.280
<i>Let's have this punishment game some other time.</i>

00:08:58.280 --> 00:09:03.850
<i>Until I can pitch a ball as great as yours.</i>

00:09:04.360 --> 00:09:07.270
<i>Goodbye, mister.</i>

00:09:17.900 --> 00:09:19.330
Strike!

00:09:19.750 --> 00:09:21.450
<i>A knuckleball, huh?</i>

00:09:24.740 --> 00:09:26.080
Strike out!

00:09:26.600 --> 00:09:30.860
<i>It must be hard when even the pitcher doesn't know where it's going.</i>

00:09:30.860 --> 00:09:34.970
<i>And if it changes like that every time, it's a magical ball.</i>

00:09:35.290 --> 00:09:38.930
Now hitting, number 55: Itao!

00:09:38.930 --> 00:09:42.850
Wow! It's Itao! Amazing!

00:09:42.850 --> 00:09:44.650
I'm really lucky!

00:09:44.650 --> 00:09:46.770
I get to see Itao live!

00:09:51.230 --> 00:09:53.170
<i>Now, what's going to happen?</i>

00:09:53.170 --> 00:09:55.150
<i>The slugger, Itao, versus the magical ball!</i>

00:09:55.150 --> 00:09:58.030
<i>I have a feeling I'll get to see an interesting duel.</i>

00:10:10.000 --> 00:10:11.850
Wow! Amazing!

00:10:11.850 --> 00:10:14.800
He went for the knuckleball right away!{juggen}

00:10:23.540 --> 00:10:24.470
Safe!

00:10:31.110 --> 00:10:35.820
Who are the Titans going to bring out as their pitcher now?

00:10:52.280 --> 00:10:53.500
<i>Gibson!</i>

00:10:54.800 --> 00:10:59.840
This is a free fansub.

00:10:54.800 --> 00:10:59.840
Not for sale or rent.

00:11:06.180 --> 00:11:08.650
Wow! They look so good!

00:11:11.180 --> 00:11:12.460
They smell nice!

00:11:12.460 --> 00:11:14.900
Just what you'd expect from real Chinese steamed buns!

00:11:14.900 --> 00:11:15.760
Really.

00:11:15.760 --> 00:11:19.930
We co-ordinated you so you'd look cute,
but if you act like that...

00:11:19.930 --> 00:11:22.720
She seems more like a "dumpling" rather than a "flower" type.

00:11:22.720 --> 00:11:24.290
Yeah. Yeah.

00:11:24.290 --> 00:11:25.830
Hi!

00:11:26.260 --> 00:11:28.160
Sorry we're late.

00:11:28.160 --> 00:11:32.590
Oh no. We just arrived ourselves.

00:11:32.590 --> 00:11:34.510
Then let's all have a nice time today.

00:11:34.510 --> 00:11:35.530
Same here.

00:11:35.530 --> 00:11:37.460
Let's have a nice time.

00:11:37.460 --> 00:11:39.780
Let's have fun on our date.

00:11:39.780 --> 00:11:40.500
Yes.

00:11:40.500 --> 00:11:43.300
Then let's go this way first.

00:11:43.300 --> 00:11:44.730
Okay.

00:11:45.550 --> 00:11:46.720
Geez!

00:11:46.720 --> 00:11:48.870
Um... Could I have a Chinese steamed bun-

00:11:48.870 --> 00:11:50.380
What are you doing, Kaoru!?

00:11:50.380 --> 00:11:51.740
You're coming too!

00:11:51.740 --> 00:11:53.520
Wait a second, Maki!

00:11:53.520 --> 00:11:56.440
Can't I have one?

00:11:58.360 --> 00:12:00.580
This one's cute!

00:12:00.580 --> 00:12:01.900
This one's cute too!

00:12:04.150 --> 00:12:05.620
This is really good!

00:12:12.530 --> 00:12:14.870
No way! Really?

00:12:14.870 --> 00:12:15.830
It's true!

00:12:15.830 --> 00:12:16.880
So that's how it was.

00:12:16.880 --> 00:12:18.650
I was really surprised!

00:12:18.650 --> 00:12:20.130
That's something.

00:12:20.130 --> 00:12:21.800
Yep. This is delicious!

00:12:21.800 --> 00:12:23.250
Isn't it?

00:12:23.250 --> 00:12:25.150
Please try some, Hayashida-san.

00:12:25.150 --> 00:12:26.260
Thank you.

00:12:34.070 --> 00:12:35.020
All right!

00:12:49.160 --> 00:12:50.160
Wow!

00:12:50.160 --> 00:12:51.670
I got it! I got it!

00:12:51.670 --> 00:12:52.450
Asami, you're amazing!

00:12:52.450 --> 00:12:53.490
Yeah, really!

00:12:54.690 --> 00:12:58.580
Ow, ow! What are you doing, Maki!?

00:12:58.580 --> 00:13:00.400
What am I doing!?

00:13:00.400 --> 00:13:05.500
We arranged this date for you and all you're doing is eating, sleeping, and yawning!

00:13:05.500 --> 00:13:07.280
What are you thinking!?

00:13:07.280 --> 00:13:09.140
But I'm bored.

00:13:09.440 --> 00:13:14.530
I'd rather be swinging away at the batting cages than be here.

00:13:14.530 --> 00:13:17.020
In that case, they have one here too.

00:13:18.060 --> 00:13:20.690
The batting cages are on the roof.

00:13:20.690 --> 00:13:21.910
You want to go together?

00:13:21.910 --> 00:13:23.930
Yeah! I'll go. I'll go!

00:13:23.930 --> 00:13:25.140
Then this way.

00:13:25.820 --> 00:13:27.490
Have a nice time!

00:13:27.490 --> 00:13:28.640
So you like baseball?

00:13:28.640 --> 00:13:29.450
Yeah, I love it!

00:13:29.860 --> 00:13:32.400
Well, in the end, it's the batting cages...

00:13:33.250 --> 00:13:34.590
Oh well.

00:13:35.240 --> 00:13:36.920
Good luck, Kaoru!

00:13:42.600 --> 00:13:46.310
You're sort of strange, Shimizu-san.

00:13:46.310 --> 00:13:48.720
Huh? How so?

00:13:48.720 --> 00:13:52.560
You become more lively once you're holding a bat.

00:13:52.560 --> 00:13:55.680
Well, I'm not used to that sort of situation.

00:14:00.210 --> 00:14:02.110
The first inning is finished.

00:14:04.600 --> 00:14:06.210
Thanks.

00:14:06.210 --> 00:14:08.000
I think this suits me best.

00:14:08.000 --> 00:14:10.680
I think this suits me best.

00:14:11.400 --> 00:14:12.730
I get it. I get it.

00:14:12.730 --> 00:14:13.430
Huh?

00:14:15.450 --> 00:14:21.780
When I was little, I used to play baseball all day too.

00:14:21.780 --> 00:14:25.350
So to be honest, I'm not used to having conversations with girls.

00:14:25.350 --> 00:14:26.670
I see.

00:14:29.220 --> 00:14:32.510
So I feel more at ease...

00:14:35.210 --> 00:14:37.040
when I'm swinging the bat like this.

00:15:02.790 --> 00:15:05.210
That was a great workout!

00:15:05.210 --> 00:15:07.450
You bat really well, Shimizu-san.

00:15:07.450 --> 00:15:09.010
As I'd expect from someone on the softball club.

00:15:09.010 --> 00:15:10.280
You too.

00:15:10.280 --> 00:15:13.100
Being the cleanup hitter on a university baseball team is amazing!

00:15:13.380 --> 00:15:19.100
But I never thought I'd be practicing batting somewhere like this.

00:15:19.100 --> 00:15:20.380
I'm sorry.

00:15:20.380 --> 00:15:22.130
I got carried away.

00:15:22.130 --> 00:15:22.980
It's cool.

00:15:22.980 --> 00:15:24.750
It was fun.

00:15:24.750 --> 00:15:26.360
R-Really?

00:15:26.780 --> 00:15:27.740
Yeah.

00:15:28.880 --> 00:15:31.660
Hey. If you'd like, would you like to come here again?

00:15:31.660 --> 00:15:33.710
That sounds great!

00:15:33.710 --> 00:15:38.580
How about we all compete and see who can hit the most?

00:15:38.580 --> 00:15:40.000
Okay?

00:15:40.000 --> 00:15:43.330
I would like it if it was just you and I, Shimizu-san.

00:15:44.840 --> 00:15:47.640
I'd like you to go on a date with me.

00:15:47.640 --> 00:15:50.080
A-A date... with me?

00:15:50.080 --> 00:15:51.180
Yeah.

00:15:51.180 --> 00:15:53.660
It's fun being with you,

00:15:53.660 --> 00:15:55.680
and I get to talk about baseball.

00:15:55.910 --> 00:15:56.610
U-Um...

00:15:56.610 --> 00:15:57.610
U-Um...

00:15:57.610 --> 00:15:58.290
That's...

00:15:58.290 --> 00:15:59.480
Well...

00:15:59.480 --> 00:16:01.170
You don't want to?

00:16:01.170 --> 00:16:04.190
No... well... How can I say this... It's...

00:16:05.330 --> 00:16:07.610
<i>What should I do!?</i>

00:16:09.670 --> 00:16:13.350
In that case, what kind of person do you like?

00:16:14.200 --> 00:16:16.060
What kind?

00:16:16.060 --> 00:16:16.910
Yeah.

00:16:17.330 --> 00:16:17.890
U-Um...

00:16:17.890 --> 00:16:19.870
U-Um...

00:16:28.210 --> 00:16:32.140
I guess someone that is chasing after a big dream.

00:16:32.140 --> 00:16:33.610
How big?

00:16:33.610 --> 00:16:38.890
Like someone that goes to challenge the Majors right after graduating from high school.

00:16:38.890 --> 00:16:41.890
The Majors? You mean <i>the</i> Majors? In America?

00:16:41.890 --> 00:16:44.060
Yeah. It was a big surprise.

00:16:44.410 --> 00:16:49.450
He has always been the type that would run straight for his goal once he decided what it was.

00:16:49.450 --> 00:16:52.730
And if he came across a wall, he'd smash straight through it.

00:16:52.730 --> 00:16:54.410
I guess he's a bit reckless.

00:16:54.410 --> 00:16:58.590
I wonder if he's still doing the same thing in America.

00:16:59.550 --> 00:17:00.270
Geez...

00:17:02.760 --> 00:17:05.920
You really like this person.

00:17:09.070 --> 00:17:11.910
But he's in America, right?

00:17:11.910 --> 00:17:12.490
Y-Yeah.

00:17:12.490 --> 00:17:13.730
Y-Yeah.

00:17:13.730 --> 00:17:16.050
Aren't you lonely since he isn't by your side?

00:17:21.140 --> 00:17:25.550
I think challenging the Majors is a great dream.

00:17:25.550 --> 00:17:31.160
But to be honest, I also think it's reckless and that he's running away from reality.

00:17:32.580 --> 00:17:35.960
If it was me, I would choose a stable life.

00:17:36.700 --> 00:17:41.210
And I would always be by your side.

00:17:47.310 --> 00:17:48.380
I'm sorry.

00:17:48.380 --> 00:17:50.020
I'm going home.

00:17:50.950 --> 00:17:52.090
Shimizu-san!

00:18:16.050 --> 00:18:16.990
Ball!

00:18:16.990 --> 00:18:18.390
That was close!

00:18:18.390 --> 00:18:20.660
He almost hit him.

00:18:23.460 --> 00:18:24.790
Strike!

00:18:24.790 --> 00:18:25.960
I get it!

00:18:25.960 --> 00:18:30.380
He threw that inside pitch on purpose to set up the next pitch outside.

00:18:33.270 --> 00:18:39.940
<i>That old man has the perfect control I'm trying to get.</i>

00:18:39.940 --> 00:18:43.180
<i>That's why he can risk going for that tactic.</i>

00:18:46.370 --> 00:18:47.730
Strike!

00:18:48.150 --> 00:18:51.900
<i>But his pitching style sure has changed.</i>

00:18:51.900 --> 00:18:54.860
<i>He used to push the batters back with his fastballs...</i>

00:18:56.980 --> 00:18:59.150
Strike out!

00:19:05.370 --> 00:19:06.540
Amazing...

00:19:06.540 --> 00:19:09.210
He held that guy with his strength in the end.

00:19:09.470 --> 00:19:13.590
That old man has increased his skills.

00:19:13.590 --> 00:19:15.250
Dammit!

00:19:15.250 --> 00:19:20.120
I need to hurry up, so I can fight him on the greatest stage!

00:19:20.120 --> 00:19:22.760
I don't have time to stay in the Minors.

00:19:27.060 --> 00:19:29.040
<i>You've become weaker, old man.</i>

00:19:29.720 --> 00:19:33.940
<i>I'm going to smash your ball into the stands when I rise up to the Majors.</i>

00:19:35.180 --> 00:19:38.940
<i>I'm going to crush your baseball beliefs.</i>

00:19:39.330 --> 00:19:41.240
<i>Completely and utterly.</i>

00:19:46.480 --> 00:19:49.200
"A stable life"!?

00:19:50.600 --> 00:19:52.580
What's wrong with chasing a dream!?

00:19:52.580 --> 00:19:56.080
The game is over when you give up on your dream!

00:19:57.590 --> 00:19:59.900
That girl is amazing.

00:19:59.900 --> 00:20:01.970
Maybe she could make it to the Majors.

00:20:03.810 --> 00:20:07.260
<i>But he's in America, right?</i>

00:20:07.260 --> 00:20:09.680
<i>Aren't you lonely {that}since he isn't by your side?</i>

00:20:19.150 --> 00:20:22.220
Of course I'm lonely...

00:20:32.760 --> 00:20:34.710
I'm back.

00:20:36.760 --> 00:20:38.000
Upsy-daisy.

00:20:39.040 --> 00:20:41.420
I'm kind of tired.

00:20:43.870 --> 00:20:46.700
Now, today's Titans game...

00:20:44.800 --> 00:20:47.910
Maki is probably angry.

00:20:46.700 --> 00:20:51.410
They're leading 4-1.

00:20:47.910 --> 00:20:50.060
I need to apologize to her later.

00:20:52.670 --> 00:20:56.170
In the top of the eighth inning, the Titans have one out and runners on first and third.

00:20:56.170 --> 00:20:57.730
The next batter is Itao.

00:20:58.130 --> 00:21:01.830
The Titans have a chance at scoring another insurance run...

00:21:00.520 --> 00:21:01.830
The Majors, huh?

00:21:04.130 --> 00:21:06.850
I wonder how he's doing.

00:21:10.970 --> 00:21:12.710
He hit it!

00:21:12.710 --> 00:21:15.990
Itao's hit stretches far, far into the right field stands!

00:21:15.990 --> 00:21:16.920
It's a home run! A home run!

00:21:16.920 --> 00:21:18.040
It's a home run! A home run!

00:21:18.040 --> 00:21:19.670
Itao hits a three-run home run!

00:21:19.960 --> 00:21:21.550
I-It's Honda!

00:21:23.850 --> 00:21:25.680
Just you wait, Gibson!

00:21:25.680 --> 00:21:28.550
I'll be there soon!

00:21:28.870 --> 00:21:35.430
Oh dear. It looks like the crowd member who caught the homer is over-excited, and he's shouting something.

00:21:36.090 --> 00:21:37.480
What an idiot.

00:21:37.480 --> 00:21:40.470
He hasn't changed, even in America.

00:21:43.580 --> 00:21:47.380
Don't come back here until you achieve your dream, Honda!

00:21:48.780 --> 00:21:50.210
This is a problem.

00:21:53.130 --> 00:21:54.620
W-What!?

00:21:54.620 --> 00:21:56.920
H-Hey, Honda!

00:21:57.080 --> 00:22:01.380
What the hell is with that {lipstick}kiss mark!?{juggen}

00:22:04.370 --> 00:22:09.080
I'm going to kill you the moment you come back!

00:22:16.750 --> 00:22:17.520
Hey.

00:22:17.920 --> 00:22:19.450
How was the game yesterday?

00:22:19.450 --> 00:22:21.420
Did you learn anything from it?

00:22:21.420 --> 00:22:22.480
Yeah.

00:22:22.700 --> 00:22:27.200
I was reminded of what I was really aiming for.

00:22:28.450 --> 00:22:29.640
I see.

00:22:29.640 --> 00:22:30.740
I'm glad.

00:22:33.410 --> 00:22:34.600
All right!

00:22:34.600 --> 00:22:37.870
Just you wait, Majors!

00:24:10.890 --> 00:24:15.520
The Memphis Bats only need one more victory to win the pennant for the first time in 15 years!

00:24:15.520 --> 00:24:16.960
15 years ago?

00:24:16.960 --> 00:24:19.980
No wonder the Bats' fans are excited.

00:24:19.980 --> 00:24:20.670
All right!

00:24:20.670 --> 00:24:21.470
We'll do it!

00:24:22.220 --> 00:24:23.400
Next time, on Major:

00:24:23.400 --> 00:24:25.190
Alice's Dream. Everyone's Dream.

00:24:25.910 --> 00:24:28.080
Run towards the stage of your dreams!
